---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import ClaimBlock from '../components/ClaimBlock.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const claim = (id: string) => release.claims.find(c => c.id === id);
const karnataka = claim('C-KA-DROUGHT-ORDER-20260922');
const funds = claim('C-JJM-FUNDS-20260331');
const heavyRain = claim('C-IMD-WEATHER-EVENT-20260924');
const threeOrders = claim('C-KA-DROUGHT-THREE-ORDERS-20260922');
const source = (id: string) => {
  const item = claim(id);
  return item ? url(`/sources/${item.evidenceIds[0]}/`) : url('/sources/');
};
---
<Site title="An order is the first step" description="The 22 September Karnataka declaration, the documented Jal Jeevan Mission programme step and the records needed to establish relief outcomes.">
  <PageHeader title="An order is the first step" eyebrow="Government response / documented stages" description="A declaration changes an administrative status. The next questions are whether relief was funded, delivered, and felt by the people it was meant to reach." />
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Karnataka / three gazettes / through 22 September 2026</p><h2>One hundred and seventy-seven taluks are listed.</h2></div></div>
    {threeOrders && <div class="grid-2"><div class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag order">Government orders · administrative count</span><strong>177</strong><p>distinct drought-affected taluks across the 27 August, 17 September and 22 September kharif 2026 gazettes: 161 severe and 16 moderate. This is not a count of people, measured crop loss or relief delivered.</p><p class="small"><a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260827/')}>27 Aug ↗</a> · <a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260917/')}>17 Sep ↗</a> · <a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260922/')}>22 Sep ↗</a></p></div><div class="g11-clock"><p class="eyebrow">How the list grew</p><p>The original annexes list 101, then 23, then 53 additional taluks; checked district–taluk pairs did not overlap. The latest <a href={karnataka ? source(karnataka.id) : url('/sources/')}>22 September order</a> takes effect immediately for up to six months unless revoked, authorizes district relief under SDRF norms and directs a joint crop-loss survey.</p><p><strong>What remains open:</strong> aid delivered, survey results and household supply. The 17 September gazette has a preamble inconsistency; its operative annex supports 21 severe and two moderate taluks. <a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260917/')}>Inspect that source ↗</a></p></div></div>}
    {heavyRain && <aside class="g11-clock"><span class="g11-tag measured">Observed event · IMD reported</span><h3>A heavy-rain event does not finish this story.</h3><p>IMD reported very heavy rain in coastal and south-interior Karnataka during the 24 hours ending 08:30 IST on 24 September. That report is a later local weather event; it neither measures crop recovery nor documents relief delivery under the 22 September order. <a href={source(heavyRain.id)}>Weather release ↗</a> <a href={karnataka ? source(karnataka.id) : url('/sources/')}>Gazette order ↗</a></p></aside>}
    <p class="g11-pull">The declaration is real. The outcome is an open question.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">How a decision becomes a result</p><h2>Follow the paper trail, stage by stage.</h2></div></div>
    <ol class="g11-sequence"><li><h3>Authority</h3><p>Find the signed orders, their geographic lists, effective dates and legal scope. <strong>Here:</strong> three Karnataka gazettes and 177 distinct listed taluks are approved. <a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260827/')}>27 Aug ↗</a> <a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260917/')}>17 Sep ↗</a> <a href={url('/sources/E-KA-GAZETTE-DROUGHT-20260922/')}>22 Sep ↗</a></p></li><li><h3>Funding and release</h3><p>Distinguish money sanctioned, money transferred and money spent. The Karnataka declaration authorizes relief but contains no verified delivery total in this publication.</p></li><li><h3>Implementation</h3><p>Check survey completion, relief distribution and service records in each named place. We have no approved delivery result for the listed taluks.</p></li><li><h3>Outcome</h3><p>Ask what households, farms and services actually experienced, with dated measures and counterevidence. A crop-loss survey being directed does not mean losses were measured.</p></li></ol>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">A separate national programme</p><h2>Jal Jeevan Mission is another record—not the Karnataka relief order.</h2></div></div>
    {funds && <div class="grid-2"><div><span class="g11-tag order">Ministry report</span><p>On 31 March 2026 the Ministry of Jal Shakti said the Union Cabinet had approved Jal Jeevan Mission 2.0 on 10 March and operational guidelines had been released on 22 March. It reported <strong>₹1,561.53 crore released to five named states</strong> for FY 2025–26. <a href={source(funds.id)}>Ministry release ↗</a></p></div><div class="g11-clock"><p class="eyebrow">Do not skip a stage</p><p>This is the ministry's account of an approval, guidelines and fund release. It is not independent treasury confirmation, state expenditure, completed work or proof of better service. It is not identified as a response to the September rainfall shortfall.</p></div></div>}
    <div class="g11-epilogue"><p class="eyebrow">A reporting path</p><h3>Which record would answer the next question?</h3><p>For Karnataka, seek the joint survey, relief orders, transfer records and district delivery evidence. For a tap-water scheme, seek the completion record and measured reliability and quality. Absence from our approved ledger is not evidence that an authority did nothing.</p><a href={url('/journalists/')}>Use the document question bank ↗</a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Exact source-linked findings</p>{threeOrders && <ClaimBlock claim={threeOrders} heading="Three Karnataka orders: 177 listed taluks" />}{karnataka && <ClaimBlock claim={karnataka} heading="22 September order: 53 additional taluks" />}{funds && <ClaimBlock claim={funds} heading="Ministry-reported JJM 2.0 step" />}</div></section>
</Site>
